{% block help_topic_content %}
<h2>What it does</h2>
<p>BM Notify replaces page-level messages with small toast notifications on AJAX responses. It provides messenger-style helpers you can call from forms or controllers, then injects the toasts into any <code>AjaxResponse</code> via its service.</p>

<h2>How to use</h2>
<ol>
  <li>Attach the library if you render notifications:
    <pre><code class="language-php">$form['#attached']['library'][] = 'bm_notify/notify';</code></pre>
  </li>
  <li>Queue messages in your code:
    <pre><code class="language-php">$notify = \Drupal::service('bm_notify');
$notify->addStatus($this->t('Saved successfully.'));
// Other types: addWarning(), addError(), addInfo(), addNotification($msg, $type, $timeout_ms)</code></pre>
  </li>
  <li>Before returning an <code>AjaxResponse</code>, append the notifications:
    <pre><code class="language-php">$notify->addToResponse($response);
return $response;</code></pre>
  </li>
</ol>

<h2>Demo</h2>
<p>Visit <code>/admin/blue-marloc/enhancements/notify-demo</code> (Blue Marloc → Enhancements → Notifications demo) to preview the toast behavior.</p>

<h2>Notes</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Works alongside Drupal messenger; use when you prefer unobtrusive toasts over page-level messages.</li>
  <li>Toast styling is in <code>css/bm-notify.css</code> and uses CSS variables (<code>--bm-notify-*</code>) for easy theming.</li>
</ul>
